From 35466ef8dbd97ac17fd1015198abc0bb14bbea22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:42:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] package.json: the docs/ modules are ESM

docs/js/*.js are ES modules, and the Node tests import them from .mjs. Without a package.json Node
guesses a .js file's type, and an ambient one above the checkout ("type": "commonjs") makes the
backup and installer tests fail on a module they cannot find a named export in. Say it here: the
tree's JavaScript is ESM. (The same patch as fm1-base's and ZEN-1's.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 package.json | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package.json

diff --git a/package.json b/package.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..019cb05
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package.json
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+{
+  "name": "tonitor",
+  "private": true,
+  "type": "module"
+}
-- 
2.55.0

